WEBVTT

00:50.258 --> 00:51.843
<i>Once upon a time,</i>

00:51.926 --> 00:55.930
<i>in the land of Manu Katche,
there lived a tribe called the Nanabu.</i>

00:56.806 --> 01:00.602
<i>The Nanabu were a peaceful people
who hated fighting.</i>

01:03.438 --> 01:07.859
<i>One day, a tribe bearing gold
came in ships.</i>

01:09.486 --> 01:12.197
<i>The tribe told the Nanabu</i>

01:13.364 --> 01:18.787
<i>that whoever possessed this thing
called "gold" would become happy.</i>

01:19.662 --> 01:23.625
<i>The Nanabu exchanged
some of their horses for the gold.</i>

01:24.626 --> 01:27.837
<i>Rumors about the gold spread quickly,</i>

01:28.338 --> 01:32.675
<i>and the Nanabu
soon gave up all of their horses.</i>

01:33.176 --> 01:38.181
<i>Not only that, they even handed over
their houses and precious land</i>

01:38.264 --> 01:41.643
<i>as advised by the gold-bearing tribe.</i>

01:42.435 --> 01:46.731
<i>The Nanabu people lost everything.</i>

01:47.273 --> 01:51.402
<i>In the end, they were driven
to Mt. Manabonzo</i>

01:52.070 --> 01:55.532
<i>and threw themselves
into its volcanic throat one by one.</i>

01:56.991 --> 02:01.412
<i>The spirits of the Nanabu people
transformed into a giant.</i>

02:02.247 --> 02:05.750
<i>That giant slumbers
deep inside the volcano,</i>

02:06.417 --> 02:10.213
and legend has it
that it will one day rise again

02:10.296 --> 02:13.800
here in Eden National Park.

02:13.883 --> 02:14.801
I see.

02:15.510 --> 02:19.305
Now, let's move on
to the local native reservation.

02:19.389 --> 02:21.641
Stay close to the flag, please.

02:34.320 --> 02:36.447
It's done. All of it.

02:37.740 --> 02:39.909
They're all dead.

02:41.119 --> 02:44.164
Yes, everything went according to plan.

02:44.873 --> 02:49.169
We have now eliminated everything
that could pose a threat to our country.

02:49.252 --> 02:51.921
Our country, Thracia,

02:52.630 --> 02:54.424
<i>will forever be prosperous!</i>

02:59.846 --> 03:01.890
This is Tse Tse Mar, the tribal elder.

03:02.891 --> 03:05.351
His role is to ward off evil
and other things.

03:08.396 --> 03:10.273
What is he mumbling?

03:10.356 --> 03:12.400
Can you translate it for us?

03:13.318 --> 03:14.861
Let's see...

03:17.071 --> 03:22.744
"An evil spirit...
lurks underneath the earth..."

03:24.037 --> 03:25.038
"Its anger

03:26.664 --> 03:29.417
shall end the world."

03:37.050 --> 03:38.635
<i>We've completed the transfer.</i>

03:39.260 --> 03:41.596
We've got maximum security here.

03:41.679 --> 03:43.640
No matter what happens, we'll be ready.

03:44.641 --> 03:46.601
"No matter what happens," huh?

03:52.357 --> 03:54.400
What do you think will happen next?

03:54.484 --> 03:55.318
Excuse me?

03:56.861 --> 03:58.571
Atom is awake.

03:59.447 --> 04:01.532
What do you think will happen next?

04:04.452 --> 04:06.120
Has Dr. Tenma been located?

04:06.204 --> 04:07.538
Not yet.

04:08.915 --> 04:09.999
What did you do,

04:11.376 --> 04:12.460
Dr. Tenma?

04:13.336 --> 04:15.380
What did you do to Atom?

04:17.173 --> 04:20.260
He said he installed a certain program.

04:20.969 --> 04:21.970
A program?

04:22.720 --> 04:23.846
What program?

04:24.347 --> 04:25.265
I don't know.

04:25.974 --> 04:29.269
But I felt it when Atom woke up.

04:29.352 --> 04:31.229
Somewhere in the world,

04:31.312 --> 04:34.482
a great sadness spread with a "boom."

04:36.359 --> 04:37.568
Minister Ochanomizu!

04:40.113 --> 04:41.823
We've got a problem! It's Atom!

04:43.283 --> 04:44.784
He said he wanted a pen,

04:44.867 --> 04:46.995
so we gave it to him. And then...

04:47.704 --> 04:48.663
My goodness!

04:48.746 --> 04:50.873
Let me go!

04:50.957 --> 04:51.791
Atom!

05:00.550 --> 05:02.510
Take her outside quickly.

05:03.011 --> 05:03.886
Yes, sir.

05:04.887 --> 05:06.597
No, let me go!

05:06.681 --> 05:11.644
No! Atom, what are you writing? Atom!

05:11.728 --> 05:14.480
Minister Ochanomizu, what is this formula?

05:14.564 --> 05:18.026
It's a plan for an Antiproton Bomb.

05:18.776 --> 05:20.820
An Antiproton Bomb?

05:20.903 --> 05:23.239
It's a formula to destroy the earth.

05:36.002 --> 05:36.961
Atom has

05:37.670 --> 05:41.174
completed a recipe for a bomb

05:42.508 --> 05:44.677
that will destroy the earth.

05:50.767 --> 05:52.435
Well, well.

05:52.518 --> 05:55.688
What an honor it is to be visited
by such a renowned roboticist.

05:57.607 --> 05:59.442
Then again, I knew you would come.

05:59.942 --> 06:01.819
Atom woke up, didn't he?

06:01.903 --> 06:04.197
Did he say, "Good morning, Dad"?

06:06.783 --> 06:09.202
So you knew. That's impressive.

06:10.370 --> 06:13.081
When artificial intelligence
like Atom wakes up,

06:13.164 --> 06:16.376
the rest of us
across the world take notice.

06:17.460 --> 06:21.839
You're the only artificial intelligence
that's comparable to Atom's.

06:21.923 --> 06:26.594
You didn't come here
to fix me up, did you?

06:28.930 --> 06:30.598
I want to ask you something.

06:31.265 --> 06:34.852
If you repair me,
I might be willing to talk.

06:44.654 --> 06:47.740
Dr. Tenma, I will not rely
on your help anymore!

06:48.241 --> 06:50.201
I will bring Atom back!

06:50.785 --> 06:52.870
Minister Ochanomizu,
we've got an emergency!

06:52.954 --> 06:53.830
Now what?

06:53.913 --> 06:56.791
Atom has escaped.

06:58.459 --> 06:59.710
I can't believe it.

07:00.211 --> 07:03.756
The walls should have stopped any attack,
yet Atom smashed right through.

07:04.465 --> 07:05.425
Where did he go?

07:05.508 --> 07:07.343
We can track him through his GPS.

07:07.427 --> 07:08.719
Request military help!

07:09.345 --> 07:11.764
No, I will handle this.

07:16.269 --> 07:20.106
He's currently in Kudanshita.
Not so far from here.

07:21.274 --> 07:24.944
Dr. Tenma, what did you do to Atom?

07:25.611 --> 07:28.364
But I knew how to wake it up.

07:29.198 --> 07:31.200
By destroying the balance.

07:31.284 --> 07:34.245
Anger, sorrow, hatred...

07:34.328 --> 07:37.081
By infusing unbalanced emotions.

07:37.165 --> 07:40.585
He said he installed a certain program.

07:44.839 --> 07:45.840
He couldn't have...

07:46.883 --> 07:51.095
You installed Gesicht's memory chip
in Atom, didn't you?

07:52.263 --> 07:53.681
Yes.

07:53.764 --> 07:56.893
The data containing the memory
of his last moments.

07:57.685 --> 08:00.354
What if the last memory
etched in the chip was

08:01.481 --> 08:03.065
of hatred?

08:26.255 --> 08:27.381
You'd better...

08:28.216 --> 08:29.967
not make me angry.

08:34.055 --> 08:35.765
Huh? What's the matter?

08:35.848 --> 08:37.350
Atom is alive...

08:37.934 --> 08:40.811
What? But weren't they all destroyed?

08:41.854 --> 08:45.733
He's alive and filled with
an incredible amount of hatred.

08:46.234 --> 08:47.109
Hatred?

08:47.860 --> 08:51.030
Don't be silly.
Robots can't hate anything.

08:52.073 --> 08:53.241
You didn't know?

08:55.201 --> 08:57.578
You thought robots can't feel anger?

08:58.246 --> 09:00.498
You thought robots can't cry?

09:02.291 --> 09:05.670
You thought robots can't feel hatred?

09:39.120 --> 09:39.954
Atom...

10:08.065 --> 10:09.191
<i>Is that a snail?</i>

10:11.235 --> 10:13.237
<i>Squads B and C, move to the south!</i>

10:13.321 --> 10:15.698
Kurt! If something happens to Kurt, I...

10:15.781 --> 10:17.908
Please! Please save my son!

10:17.992 --> 10:20.119
Sir, ma'am, please calm down.

10:21.078 --> 10:22.622
Where are the reinforcements?

10:26.125 --> 10:28.919
I'm Gesicht of Europol.
What is the situation?

10:29.545 --> 10:32.048
The perpetrator doesn't seem
open to negotiations.

10:32.548 --> 10:34.383
He's barricaded himself up ahead.

10:35.301 --> 10:36.677
What weapons does he have?

10:36.761 --> 10:39.555
A recoilless MMG. Military grade.

10:40.556 --> 10:42.433
He's up ahead, behind that structure.

10:58.366 --> 10:59.867
Be quiet, brat!

11:02.203 --> 11:03.037
Drop your gun!

11:03.120 --> 11:04.789
Don't come any closer!

11:05.581 --> 11:08.334
If you do, I'll shoot him! I mean it!

11:09.460 --> 11:10.461
You must be Kurt.

11:12.463 --> 11:14.674
I'm a robot policeman.

11:14.757 --> 11:18.469
This electromagnetic gun
will only hit the bad guy.

11:18.552 --> 11:20.429
I promise it won't hit you.

11:20.513 --> 11:21.972
Hey, didn't you hear me?

11:22.473 --> 11:26.602
But I need you to stay perfectly still.

11:28.854 --> 11:29.814
Kurt!

11:30.981 --> 11:33.567
Think of the people you love the most.

11:34.360 --> 11:36.237
The people I love the most?

11:36.320 --> 11:38.030
That will give you courage.

11:38.114 --> 11:41.117
Shut up! I'll blow his head off!

11:42.118 --> 11:43.786
Mommy...

11:44.578 --> 11:45.413
Daddy...

11:45.496 --> 11:46.622
Good job.

11:47.123 --> 11:51.293
Mommy, Daddy...

11:51.377 --> 11:53.546
Very good, Kurt. You're being very strong.

11:53.629 --> 11:57.717
Mommy, Daddy...

12:11.397 --> 12:12.314
Suspect secured!

12:16.110 --> 12:17.778
You did great, Kurt.

12:18.279 --> 12:20.781
Kurt!

12:20.865 --> 12:22.283
Kurt!

12:22.366 --> 12:23.242
Kurt!

12:23.325 --> 12:24.452
Kurt!

12:25.202 --> 12:27.580
Mommy! Daddy!

12:30.875 --> 12:33.919
Thank goodness you're safe, Kurt!

12:34.003 --> 12:34.837
Kurt!

12:35.337 --> 12:36.839
I won't ever let you go again!

12:37.339 --> 12:40.468
I won't ever let you go,
even if the world ends!

12:55.816 --> 12:59.862
"I won't ever let you go,
even if the world ends," huh?

13:06.076 --> 13:08.162
Hey, you there! Out of the way!

13:08.245 --> 13:09.747
Oh, sorry.

13:18.589 --> 13:22.384
Jeez, the guy had to make a scene here,
of all places.

13:22.468 --> 13:24.887
I've lost a whole day of business.

13:27.389 --> 13:32.102
I'd better check for recyclable parts
before I start crushing it.

13:33.687 --> 13:37.107
I might make a fair amount
if I sell the parts to a robot hospital.

13:40.945 --> 13:42.071
Excuse me!

13:42.154 --> 13:43.447
Hold on a second!

13:43.531 --> 13:44.406
Huh?

13:57.753 --> 13:58.587
It's moving.

14:00.881 --> 14:02.383
This robot is still alive.

14:07.680 --> 14:11.225
Nah, it's far too gone to call it alive.

14:11.851 --> 14:15.187
It's quite an old model too.
There's nothing usable left.

14:16.647 --> 14:18.941
It'll just have to be crushed.

14:19.024 --> 14:19.942
I'll take it.

14:35.291 --> 14:36.125
Excuse me.

14:37.084 --> 14:38.210
This child...

14:38.294 --> 14:39.128
"Child"?

14:42.590 --> 14:43.799
May I have it?

14:43.883 --> 14:45.968
Sure. Fine with me.

14:46.552 --> 14:48.012
It's just junk.

14:53.267 --> 14:56.228
You can have the whole body for 500 ZEUS.

14:58.731 --> 14:59.565
Helena.

15:00.649 --> 15:02.526
I'm on my way home.

15:03.235 --> 15:05.029
I've got a surprise for you.

15:06.614 --> 15:09.241
What is it?
You'll just have to wait and see.

15:09.867 --> 15:11.243
I know you'll love it.

15:12.745 --> 15:13.871
I'll be home soon.

15:15.122 --> 15:15.956
Yes.

15:24.423 --> 15:25.257
He walked...

15:25.966 --> 15:27.468
He walked, Gesicht.

15:27.551 --> 15:28.385
Yes!

15:29.303 --> 15:32.348
That's right. You're doing great!
Just a little more!

15:33.140 --> 15:34.975
Is this really our child?

15:35.935 --> 15:37.728
Yes, this is our child.

15:38.562 --> 15:39.480
He's alive.

15:40.230 --> 15:42.441
This child is alive!

15:43.275 --> 15:48.113
I finally understand
what it means to be alive.

15:51.784 --> 15:54.828
This is what it means to live.

15:55.496 --> 15:56.664
Pa... pa...

15:57.998 --> 15:59.291
Ma... ma...

16:01.460 --> 16:03.754
We must give our child a name.

16:04.588 --> 16:05.673
You're right.

16:08.300 --> 16:09.134
Robita.

16:09.635 --> 16:10.469
How about it?

16:11.095 --> 16:12.096
Robita.

16:13.138 --> 16:14.556
What a beautiful name.

16:15.307 --> 16:18.852
I won't ever let you go,
even if the world ends.

16:26.235 --> 16:27.111
Stop!

16:31.824 --> 16:33.158
I was wrong!

16:33.242 --> 16:34.827
I...

16:36.203 --> 16:38.080
Please spare me!

16:42.626 --> 16:44.086
Please don't!

16:49.675 --> 16:50.968
Don't shoot me!

17:06.150 --> 17:06.984
Gesicht.

17:07.568 --> 17:10.029
Mr. Haas, there's something
I want to ask you.

17:11.447 --> 17:13.699
Does the hatred you humans feel
ever disappear?

17:14.450 --> 17:15.617
Or does it never go away,

17:16.118 --> 17:18.746
no matter how many times
you try to erase it?

17:22.166 --> 17:24.251
What I am most afraid of

17:25.294 --> 17:29.423
is myself, now that I've learned
how to hate.

17:30.007 --> 17:30.883
What?

17:37.723 --> 17:38.557
Wait!

17:43.479 --> 17:47.316
I don't know
whether the hatred can go away.

17:48.150 --> 17:49.068
But...

17:53.447 --> 17:56.241
my hatred is...

18:16.470 --> 18:18.347
What's wrong, Ali?

18:19.264 --> 18:22.935
You heard the gunshot, right?
It's dangerous here.

18:23.018 --> 18:24.561
Come this way.

18:26.146 --> 18:28.899
You know, I have a little one like you.

18:34.113 --> 18:34.947
Ali!

18:36.156 --> 18:38.242
What's wrong, Ali?

18:48.085 --> 18:49.711
Nothing will be born from this...

18:53.340 --> 18:57.594
Nothing comes from hatred...

19:31.211 --> 19:32.129
Atom.

19:33.005 --> 19:33.881
You...

19:39.845 --> 19:41.096
I'm all right now.

19:41.638 --> 19:42.890
Professor Ochanomizu.

19:54.401 --> 19:55.777
Atom, my boy.

20:00.407 --> 20:02.910
<i>The hatred is gone.</i>

20:04.494 --> 20:08.332
<i>Hatred and sorrow never fade.</i>

20:09.917 --> 20:13.921
You may think they have passed,
but they continue to burn silently.

20:16.089 --> 20:17.382
That's for sure.

20:18.342 --> 20:20.344
But I want to ask you something.

20:20.844 --> 20:22.679
That's why I came here.

20:23.972 --> 20:25.515
Where's Abullah?

20:26.225 --> 20:28.310
I have a responsibility to stop all this.

20:28.936 --> 20:31.271
You don't need to look for him.

20:32.981 --> 20:35.025
He will find you.

20:49.122 --> 20:51.500
- Sorry to have kept you waiting.
- Not at all.

20:52.042 --> 20:53.377
To the airport, please.

20:53.460 --> 20:54.461
Yes, sir.

21:06.682 --> 21:08.767
<i>Go ahead and tell us, Atom.</i>

21:09.393 --> 21:13.730
Okay. Gesicht's memory chip
was installed in me.

21:14.731 --> 21:16.275
What I'm about to tell you

21:16.775 --> 21:19.695
are the full details
of what his investigation uncovered.

21:21.029 --> 21:23.991
<i>When Darius XIV was dictator
of the Kingdom of Persia,</i>

21:24.574 --> 21:29.413
<i>he developed a plan to quickly turn
his desert kingdom into fertile land.</i>

21:30.205 --> 21:36.378
<i>And he asked Professor Abullah
to create an earth-altering robot.</i>

21:37.587 --> 21:39.589
This plan was called the Bora Project.

21:40.173 --> 21:42.592
So it wasn't a weapon of mass destruction?

21:43.093 --> 21:46.054
Right. At least not in the beginning.

21:46.763 --> 21:49.850
But the Bora Project
was faced with many setbacks.

21:49.933 --> 21:53.770
Each prototype Professor Abullah created
failed and was discarded.

21:54.354 --> 21:56.815
That's what Professor Ochanomizu
and the others found.

21:57.524 --> 21:59.568
Oh, the graveyard of robots.

22:02.696 --> 22:05.574
Then, Professor Abullah
came up with an idea.

22:06.325 --> 22:08.118
In order to complete the Bora Project,

22:08.201 --> 22:12.122
he realized he needed a capable assistant
whose abilities surpassed those of humans.

22:12.914 --> 22:15.250
"Abilities surpassing those of humans..."

22:15.334 --> 22:17.169
"A capable assistant..."

22:17.252 --> 22:20.255
A robot with the most advanced
artificial intelligence.

22:21.923 --> 22:25.969
To achieve that goal,
a certain scientist was invited to Persia.

22:26.511 --> 22:27.721
A certain scientist?

22:30.640 --> 22:31.850
Dr. Tenma.

22:31.933 --> 22:32.768
Tenma?

22:47.532 --> 22:48.700
Where am I?

22:50.452 --> 22:52.621
I heard Atom has been revived.

22:53.747 --> 22:56.124
So it was you, after all, Abullah.

22:57.376 --> 22:59.628
It is good to see you, Dr. Tenma.

23:00.337 --> 23:03.507
So you kidnapped me as bait
to lure Atom here?

23:04.007 --> 23:04.841
No.

23:07.761 --> 23:09.930
There's no more need for that.

23:11.348 --> 23:12.265
Then why?

23:13.141 --> 23:14.226
This is why.

23:19.439 --> 23:20.649
Is this...

23:22.818 --> 23:24.444
Is this Pluto?

23:25.404 --> 23:27.280
No, this is Bora.

23:28.198 --> 23:31.701
A masterpiece created
by a genius scientist named Goji.

23:32.702 --> 23:37.332
My plan is to transplant my brain
into Bora here

23:38.125 --> 23:41.420
and create
the world's most sophisticated cyborg.

23:45.465 --> 23:48.009
You are the only one
who can make it happen.

23:48.093 --> 23:51.304
The only human as capable as me.

23:53.932 --> 23:57.686
<i>Professor Abullah
lost his entire family in the war.</i>

23:58.395 --> 24:00.689
He grieved for them
from the bottom of his heart,

24:02.149 --> 24:03.900
<i>and he began to hate the world.</i>

24:05.777 --> 24:07.571
A capable human, huh?

24:08.613 --> 24:10.949
Abullah, you are not human.

24:12.701 --> 24:13.660
<i>And</i>

24:14.453 --> 24:17.372
the professor himself
was killed in the war.

24:17.456 --> 24:19.958
Wait a minute. That can't be right!

24:20.041 --> 24:22.836
We just saw him a little while ago!

24:23.962 --> 24:26.047
You are not a human.

24:27.924 --> 24:29.509
What are you talking about?

24:30.218 --> 24:33.680
Since I lost most of my body in the war,

24:33.763 --> 24:35.974
I guess one could say
I'm close to a cyborg.

24:36.057 --> 24:37.684
Not a cyborg.

24:37.767 --> 24:38.685
You're a robot.

24:39.352 --> 24:41.396
Don't be ridiculous.

24:42.189 --> 24:45.192
I've known you for a long time.

24:46.318 --> 24:47.360
Because you are

24:47.903 --> 24:50.655
a robot that I created.

24:51.490 --> 24:52.866
What nonsense.

24:52.949 --> 24:55.994
Abullah asked me to create a robot.

24:56.661 --> 24:58.455
A perfect robot.

24:59.247 --> 25:02.751
But the artificial intelligence
of that robot was too advanced,

25:02.834 --> 25:04.085
so it didn't wake up.

25:04.628 --> 25:05.462
However...

25:12.928 --> 25:14.846
Dr. Tenma, you must go to the airport now!

25:15.555 --> 25:16.932
It's not safe here!

25:17.015 --> 25:17.849
I know!

25:17.933 --> 25:21.061
Dr. Tenma! I have terrible news.

25:21.645 --> 25:25.857
Professor Abullah died
in the bombing of the Timur region.

25:26.942 --> 25:28.026
You've verified this?

25:28.652 --> 25:31.238
We rescued the professor from the debris,

25:31.738 --> 25:34.032
but he died soon after.

25:38.703 --> 25:42.374
<i>Dr. Tenma listen to me.</i>

25:43.208 --> 25:48.129
<i>This contains a copy
of a certain part of my brain.</i>

25:48.797 --> 25:51.216
<i>Dr. Tenma, I know you can...</i>

25:53.677 --> 25:55.470
He left this for you.

26:02.936 --> 26:06.064
This contains Abullah's hatred.

26:07.274 --> 26:08.858
He wanted me to install it in you.

26:14.239 --> 26:15.699
The bombs are getting closer!

26:36.553 --> 26:37.596
That face...

26:39.806 --> 26:41.391
You mean to say...

26:41.474 --> 26:44.185
The man we met who called himself Abullah...

26:52.736 --> 26:54.362
That's you.

26:54.863 --> 26:55.697
You lie.

26:56.698 --> 26:57.574
A lie?

26:58.283 --> 26:59.200
Right.

27:00.285 --> 27:01.995
I'll tell you one more thing.

27:02.495 --> 27:06.124
The most advanced
artificial intelligence can lie.

27:06.791 --> 27:09.919
It can lie to others,
as well as to itself.

27:12.797 --> 27:14.466
The genius scientist Goji...

27:15.050 --> 27:16.551
He does not exist.

27:17.052 --> 27:18.345
You are Goji.

27:20.889 --> 27:22.849
Goji is Abullah.

27:23.642 --> 27:26.269
A robot with a dual personality was born.

27:26.353 --> 27:28.063
I am Goji?

27:28.647 --> 27:31.733
That's a lie...

27:31.816 --> 27:34.194
Then where is Goji?

27:35.612 --> 27:38.156
You don't need me to do a transplant.

27:38.782 --> 27:40.867
Your artificial intelligence

27:40.950 --> 27:43.620
has already been transferred
to several other robots.

27:45.705 --> 27:50.085
You lie! You're a liar!

27:50.168 --> 27:51.711
It's time to stop this.

27:51.795 --> 27:55.048
The world fully understands
your suffering now.

28:10.980 --> 28:14.526
<i>After showing the truth of life
to the king of ancient Uzbek,</i>

28:15.110 --> 28:18.988
the legendary sage of the sand
turned back into clay.

28:19.906 --> 28:21.157
<i>The name of that sage</i>

28:21.991 --> 28:22.826
<i>was Goji.</i>

28:24.786 --> 28:27.455
I am the only person who can save you.

28:28.998 --> 28:30.834
<i>Abullah created Pluto,</i>

28:31.584 --> 28:35.213
<i>and Goji created Bora,
just as they had planned.</i>

28:36.381 --> 28:39.759
<i>Pluto inherited Abullah's hatred.</i>

28:40.927 --> 28:44.597
And he hated us,
the world's seven most advanced robots.

28:45.098 --> 28:46.307
So what happened to Bora?

28:57.068 --> 28:57.944
Oh no.

29:05.535 --> 29:09.873
<i>Bora is no longer a robot
designed to produce plant life.</i>

29:10.457 --> 29:12.876
Now, he's a weapon of mass destruction.

29:12.959 --> 29:15.003
We must inform the whole world!

29:15.628 --> 29:17.672
Even if you do, there's nowhere to run.

29:17.756 --> 29:18.590
What?

29:19.466 --> 29:22.051
The whole earth will be destroyed.

29:45.533 --> 29:49.704
I hereby declare the 108th
Military Tribunal to be in session.

29:50.288 --> 29:51.956
Swear in the defendant.

30:00.215 --> 30:03.134
<i>Do not be unnerved
by a little earthquake like this.</i>

30:04.761 --> 30:06.638
What in the world is this data?

30:08.181 --> 30:09.724
This is terrible!

30:11.142 --> 30:13.478
The whole earth could be...

30:13.561 --> 30:17.190
<i>The end of everything shall begin soon.</i>

30:18.024 --> 30:19.984
Darius XIV!

30:20.068 --> 30:22.195
The defendant is not authorized to speak!

30:23.112 --> 30:27.784
<i>However, this is not my doing.
I did not cause this.</i>

30:27.867 --> 30:28.701
Silence!

30:29.828 --> 30:32.372
<i>Hatred caused this.</i>

30:48.346 --> 30:50.223
Please don't, Your Majesty.

30:53.268 --> 30:56.145
Now is not the time to take your life.

30:56.813 --> 30:58.481
Don't try to stop me, Abullah.

30:58.565 --> 31:00.942
Your Majesty, may I show you something?

31:06.489 --> 31:08.867
Pluto... So it's finally complete!

31:09.367 --> 31:11.578
Use this to kill them all.

31:11.661 --> 31:14.747
Kill all seven of the cursed robots!

31:15.373 --> 31:16.541
Leave it to me.

31:17.041 --> 31:19.794
I will take care of
the Bora Inquiry Commission as well.

31:20.295 --> 31:22.714
But the worst of the wrongdoers
is Thracia.

31:23.339 --> 31:26.050
However, there's nothing
we can do about them.

31:26.551 --> 31:28.344
Yes, there is, sir.

31:30.638 --> 31:34.517
It can be done. I can make it happen.

31:35.310 --> 31:37.687
Silence!

31:37.770 --> 31:40.231
<i>Hatred caused all of this.</i>

31:41.274 --> 31:43.401
<i>No one can escape.</i>

31:48.364 --> 31:49.240
Huh?

31:49.324 --> 31:50.325
A huge eruption?

31:50.408 --> 31:52.118
Yes, Mr. President.

31:52.201 --> 31:54.537
An eruption is almost certain.

31:54.621 --> 31:56.664
Where? How big?

31:56.748 --> 31:59.167
Our weather robot can give you details.

31:59.250 --> 32:00.877
Arnold, at your service.

32:02.295 --> 32:05.882
A robot predicting volcano eruptions?
Now that's something.

32:06.382 --> 32:09.093
Thanks to you, many lives will be saved.

32:09.177 --> 32:14.557
Mr. President, I'm afraid
many lives may not be saved.

32:15.183 --> 32:16.100
Hmm?

32:16.184 --> 32:17.602
The eruption will take place

32:19.062 --> 32:21.022
<i>in Eden National Park.</i>

32:23.608 --> 32:24.817
It's close.

32:25.610 --> 32:28.488
The time of awakening is near.

32:34.869 --> 32:38.289
There are no volcanoes
in Eden National Park.

32:38.915 --> 32:42.585
However, there is a huge pool of magma
eight kilometers below the surface.

32:43.086 --> 32:45.546
This pool contains
3,000 cubic kilometers of magma

32:46.047 --> 32:48.883
that rises and falls
due to the movement of ore-forming fluid.

32:49.384 --> 32:50.718
What is it doing now?

32:50.802 --> 32:52.011
It's rising.

32:52.845 --> 32:54.013
And its eruption cycle?

32:54.597 --> 32:56.724
Approximately once every 5,000 years.

32:56.808 --> 32:58.476
When was the last eruption?

32:58.559 --> 33:00.687
It was 5,200 years ago.

33:03.606 --> 33:05.733
What happens if it does erupt?

33:06.275 --> 33:09.904
It will eject 100 million tons
of cinder and ash per hour,

33:10.488 --> 33:12.573
and pyroclastic flow will decimate areas

33:12.657 --> 33:15.159
within a several-hundred-kilometer radius.

33:15.660 --> 33:18.746
The temperature of pyroclastic flow
is about 700 degrees Celsius,

33:18.830 --> 33:21.541
and its speed can reach
300 kilometers per hour.

33:23.376 --> 33:28.131
The ejected volcanic ash will immediately
fly 50 kilometers into the stratosphere,

33:28.214 --> 33:30.133
covering the entire planet.

33:30.967 --> 33:35.138
Several hundred million tons of ash
will block out the sun.

33:35.722 --> 33:37.223
Plants will wither away,

33:39.058 --> 33:43.855
and after a long period of acid rain,
an extreme cryogenic phase will begin.

33:44.689 --> 33:48.985
In a few months,
most biological life will be dead.

33:50.945 --> 33:54.574
And you think
this worst-case scenario will happen now?

33:55.074 --> 33:57.410
Under normal circumstances, no.

33:57.493 --> 33:58.578
- What?
- What?

33:59.078 --> 34:01.539
The magma pool is definitely rising,

34:01.622 --> 34:04.459
but the caldera is not at the state
where it should open,

34:04.542 --> 34:06.961
so a cataclysmic eruption
shouldn't be triggered.

34:09.005 --> 34:10.965
Jeez, why the commotion, then?

34:11.049 --> 34:13.718
Giving us all that doomsday talk...

34:13.801 --> 34:14.635
However...

34:16.679 --> 34:20.850
if something artificial
was heading toward the magma pool...

34:22.351 --> 34:23.436
What is this?

34:23.936 --> 34:25.980
It's my simulation.

34:26.064 --> 34:29.442
For example,
if this were an Antiproton Bomb...

34:32.195 --> 34:33.905
An Antiproton Bomb.

34:36.532 --> 34:39.744
<i>We have a problem, Mr. President!
Just now, at the military tribunal.</i>

34:40.328 --> 34:42.246
<i>No one will escape.</i>

34:42.747 --> 34:46.834
<i>A huge bomb will erupt
right below Thracia.</i>

34:55.259 --> 34:57.762
Hello there. What's the matter?

34:58.471 --> 34:59.806
Don't tell me you...

35:00.640 --> 35:02.683
Yes, I knew.

35:03.184 --> 35:06.270
Why did you keep something
so important from me?

35:06.771 --> 35:08.981
That weather-forecasting robot...

35:10.149 --> 35:13.569
He didn't have to pretend
like he was so alarmed.

35:13.653 --> 35:14.654
"Pretend"?

35:14.737 --> 35:17.031
Didn't he tell you?

35:17.115 --> 35:19.909
Most "biological life" will die.

35:21.828 --> 35:24.413
We robots will survive.

35:27.166 --> 35:28.209
Don't worry.

35:28.709 --> 35:32.380
About 10% of the earth's population
will survive too.

35:33.047 --> 35:37.385
Those remaining humans
are my gift to you, Mr. President.

35:39.262 --> 35:41.889
<i>That's the story, Professor Ochanomizu.</i>

35:42.473 --> 35:44.809
The whole earth would explode...

35:45.351 --> 35:47.103
This is what you meant, Atom?

35:47.186 --> 35:48.146
Yes.

35:48.646 --> 35:52.441
Hold on! When is this explosion
going to happen?

35:56.154 --> 35:59.031
If it continues to move
at its current rate,

35:59.115 --> 36:03.786
Bora will arrive at Eden National Park
in about 72 hours.

36:04.328 --> 36:05.997
<i>Impressive, Professor Ochanomizu.</i>

36:06.581 --> 36:09.250
But how do we know it won't speed up?

36:09.792 --> 36:12.128
I think the professor's prediction
is accurate.

36:12.795 --> 36:14.005
How do you know?

36:17.800 --> 36:19.510
Seventy-two hours from now,

36:19.594 --> 36:24.140
<i>it will have been exactly four years
since Professor Abullah lost his family.</i>

36:24.640 --> 36:27.977
I see. The anniversary
of the birth of hatred...

36:28.561 --> 36:30.688
<i>Is there no way to stop it?</i>

36:31.230 --> 36:33.941
Bora is moving quite deep
beneath the ground.

36:34.734 --> 36:39.405
<i>There is nothing else on earth
that could reach that deep.</i>

36:40.281 --> 36:42.158
If a chance exists,

36:42.241 --> 36:46.746
it would be when Bora approaches
the surface to induce the eruption.

36:47.705 --> 36:49.165
If it comes to that,

36:49.248 --> 36:51.959
then the only robot who can stop Bora is...

36:57.924 --> 36:59.050
Leave it to me.

37:00.760 --> 37:01.594
Atom...

37:05.348 --> 37:07.391
But before that,

37:08.976 --> 37:10.895
<i>there is something I must do.</i>

37:13.397 --> 37:16.651
Well, well. It's been a long time.

37:17.276 --> 37:19.862
So happy to see you, my friend.

37:20.821 --> 37:23.199
I came here today to ask a favor of you.

37:23.824 --> 37:27.036
Is that so? I have something
I wanted to ask you as well.

37:27.787 --> 37:30.206
What do you plan to do with that formula?

37:30.831 --> 37:32.041
So you know about it?

37:32.583 --> 37:34.085
I caught them right away,

37:34.710 --> 37:39.674
those strange brain waves
you were emitting as you worked.

37:40.675 --> 37:41.759
I regret doing it.

37:42.593 --> 37:44.262
After I woke up in the lab,

37:44.345 --> 37:48.015
I succumbed to the waves of hatred
that were swirling all over the world.

37:48.516 --> 37:51.352
The enemy must have noticed it as well.

37:52.645 --> 37:53.604
Yes.

37:53.688 --> 37:56.357
That's why I've come to ask you this.

37:57.400 --> 38:00.069
You mean the other threat.

38:17.128 --> 38:20.464
I will carry out your request.

38:21.716 --> 38:24.010
Thank you very much.

38:25.886 --> 38:26.721
Atom.

38:29.515 --> 38:31.642
May I touch you?

38:50.536 --> 38:51.912
You're warm.

38:53.122 --> 38:56.625
Atom, you are so...

38:57.752 --> 39:00.629
So this is a heart.

39:08.637 --> 39:09.847
How gorgeous.

39:10.348 --> 39:12.475
It looks like a completely new home!

39:13.267 --> 39:16.187
We're so glad we chose you, Helena.

39:16.270 --> 39:19.148
I'm pleased that you like it.

39:19.899 --> 39:22.234
We've dreamed of living
in a house like this, right?

39:22.318 --> 39:23.319
Yes.

39:24.403 --> 39:27.198
I'll check back with you later
about the landscaping.

39:28.032 --> 39:28.949
Thank you.

39:46.425 --> 39:47.426
Gesicht.

39:57.311 --> 39:58.187
Atom.

40:00.523 --> 40:01.649
You must be Helena.

40:02.608 --> 40:06.612
You have Gesicht inside you, don't you?

40:07.488 --> 40:10.574
Yes. Thanks to him,
I was able to come back.

40:26.549 --> 40:27.383
Thank you.

40:30.469 --> 40:32.263
Thank you, Atom.

40:32.972 --> 40:34.932
- I came to tell you something.
- Huh?

40:35.015 --> 40:38.811
Gesicht was always thinking about you.

40:39.562 --> 40:42.815
Until the very last moment,
he wanted to see you.

40:46.819 --> 40:48.779
So despite what happened to him,

40:49.280 --> 40:50.906
you'll never be alone.

40:57.872 --> 40:58.998
Thank you, Atom.

40:59.748 --> 41:02.084
You're trying to cheer me up, aren't you?

41:02.960 --> 41:03.919
It's the truth.

41:04.420 --> 41:06.338
Robots can't lie, remember?

41:07.840 --> 41:08.757
You're right.

41:09.467 --> 41:10.759
I almost forgot.

41:11.552 --> 41:13.971
It's strange of me to cry so much
when I'm a robot.

41:14.472 --> 41:15.306
Not at all.

41:17.766 --> 41:20.644
May I ask you a question?

41:20.728 --> 41:21.604
Of course.

41:21.687 --> 41:24.064
Gesicht and I realized
we were both missing memories

41:24.565 --> 41:27.902
from the same period of time.

41:28.903 --> 41:32.948
I still can't remember
what those missing memories are.

41:33.949 --> 41:35.159
But Gesicht...

41:35.659 --> 41:38.579
I keep wondering
if he might have found out what they were.

41:40.372 --> 41:43.959
Do you know
what our missing memories are about?

41:44.793 --> 41:47.421
No, Gesicht didn't know
anything about that.

41:48.797 --> 41:50.758
Are you hiding something?

41:51.258 --> 41:52.092
I am not.

41:52.176 --> 41:56.096
I'm prepared to take on any sorrow,
no matter how big it may be.

41:56.180 --> 41:57.389
Please tell me everything.

42:01.185 --> 42:03.354
No, I've told you everything I know.

42:06.565 --> 42:07.399
I see.

42:09.276 --> 42:10.194
You're leaving?

42:10.819 --> 42:11.654
Yes.

42:15.616 --> 42:16.450
Atom.

42:19.495 --> 42:21.830
Can I see you again?

42:22.665 --> 42:23.791
Of course.

42:38.514 --> 42:40.516
Robots can't lie.

42:41.767 --> 42:42.643
Atom,

42:43.435 --> 42:46.689
you just lied to me now.

42:55.447 --> 42:56.282
Thank you.

42:58.867 --> 42:59.702
Thank you.

43:00.536 --> 43:01.412
Atom.

43:06.333 --> 43:08.669
Gesicht, the time has come.

43:09.962 --> 43:11.755
I've paid my respects to everyone.

43:12.590 --> 43:15.134
I've let them know
this will be the end of everything.

43:20.806 --> 43:22.266
It's about to begin.

43:24.935 --> 43:26.186
I have to go now.

43:26.979 --> 43:28.856
Goodbye, Gesicht.

44:24.453 --> 44:26.455
Pluto!

45:03.534 --> 45:05.494
I'm going to destroy you!

45:12.710 --> 45:15.045
You may be filled with hatred...

45:17.756 --> 45:20.718
but my hatred is greater than yours.

45:23.470 --> 45:24.346
Atom.

45:25.764 --> 45:27.850
Don't do it. Atom!

45:28.934 --> 45:32.062
Mont Blanc loved the forests.

45:33.480 --> 45:36.108
<i>He tried to protect
the forests of Switzerland.</i>

45:36.608 --> 45:37.943
<i>He didn't want to die.</i>

45:39.528 --> 45:42.364
<i>North No.2 never wanted to fight again.</i>

45:43.282 --> 45:45.159
<i>He loved music.</i>

45:45.784 --> 45:48.078
<i>He didn't want to die either.</i>

45:48.787 --> 45:51.331
But you...

45:52.207 --> 45:53.333
Yes, that's right.

45:53.917 --> 45:55.586
I killed them!

46:04.553 --> 46:05.846
Brando.

46:06.722 --> 46:10.142
<i>He loved his family
and believed in the future.</i>

46:11.101 --> 46:13.645
<i>Brando and Hercules were rivals,</i>

46:14.146 --> 46:17.649
<i>but they were united by a friendship
stronger than any!</i>

46:17.733 --> 46:21.028
I'm certain that both of them

46:22.362 --> 46:26.575
didn't want to die!

46:34.208 --> 46:38.712
Epsilon was against the war so much
that he refused conscription.

46:39.296 --> 46:44.802
<i>He tried to give his love to the children
who lost everything in the war!</i>

46:45.677 --> 46:47.554
He didn't want to die!

47:01.735 --> 47:04.822
And inside me is Gesicht's...

47:07.699 --> 47:09.576
hatred!

47:12.120 --> 47:13.539
Stop it, Atom!

47:13.622 --> 47:16.041
Pluto isn't using his tornado!

47:16.124 --> 47:18.252
There is still a kind heart inside of him!

47:19.545 --> 47:20.546
I'm going too!

47:21.046 --> 47:24.758
Wait, Uran! You can't be of any help!

47:24.842 --> 47:26.927
But if we don't do something, Atom will--

47:27.010 --> 47:28.220
It's all right.

47:28.303 --> 47:31.890
Atom is strong. He won't lose so easily!

47:31.974 --> 47:34.059
- What if it's too strong?
- What?

47:34.142 --> 47:37.145
Too strong,
and there's no telling what he'll do!

47:39.189 --> 47:43.277
If his hatred or sorrow are too strong,
then Atom could...

47:43.986 --> 47:45.571
He could kill!

47:47.239 --> 47:48.532
We have to believe.

47:49.116 --> 47:51.869
That's all we can do.

47:52.578 --> 47:55.664
Atom is not that kind of boy.

48:00.210 --> 48:02.671
We're 75 kilometers
from Atom's GPS signal!

48:03.171 --> 48:04.548
Atom...

48:05.632 --> 48:08.844
You will pay for this!

48:21.315 --> 48:22.149
<i>Atom...</i>

48:29.698 --> 48:30.532
<i>Atom...</i>

48:38.749 --> 48:39.708
<i>Atom...</i>

48:46.506 --> 48:47.341
<i>Atom...</i>

48:54.014 --> 48:54.848
<i>Atom...</i>

48:59.269 --> 49:00.103
<i>Atom.</i>

49:00.938 --> 49:04.483
<i>Nothing comes from hatred.</i>

49:24.419 --> 49:25.253
Everyone,

49:25.921 --> 49:27.547
it's just as you all say...

49:37.516 --> 49:38.350
Pluto.

49:41.728 --> 49:44.022
What is this?

49:48.026 --> 49:50.654
What is this?

50:03.458 --> 50:04.334
Pluto.

50:04.876 --> 50:07.254
No, you're Sahad.

50:09.256 --> 50:10.799
I don't know why either.

50:11.925 --> 50:14.261
Why do these fall?

50:15.012 --> 50:16.346
I don't understand.

50:31.611 --> 50:32.654
A shooting star.

50:33.697 --> 50:36.491
Humans say that if they wish
upon a shooting star,

50:36.992 --> 50:38.535
their dreams will come true.

50:41.913 --> 50:43.415
Did you make a wish?

50:45.250 --> 50:46.376
I did.

50:53.383 --> 50:55.761
What did you wish for?

50:56.595 --> 50:58.221
Probably the same as you.

51:01.391 --> 51:02.267
It's time.

51:04.061 --> 51:04.936
Sahad,

51:05.479 --> 51:06.897
I have to go.

51:06.980 --> 51:10.192
Go where, Atom?

51:37.469 --> 51:41.264
Eden National Park is
in an extremely dangerous state right now.

51:41.348 --> 51:42.974
I don't care. We're landing!

51:43.058 --> 51:46.186
But, Professor Ochanomizu...

51:46.269 --> 51:47.687
Where does Atom's GPS show?

51:48.313 --> 51:50.148
He was around here until a minute ago.

51:50.732 --> 51:53.276
You don't suppose that Pluto could have...

51:53.360 --> 51:57.405
<i>Atom is no longer as weak as you think</i>

51:58.073 --> 52:00.867
<i>because I infused him
with unbalanced emotions.</i>

52:01.493 --> 52:02.536
Dr. Tenma!

52:03.036 --> 52:05.997
<i>Pluto may have been killed by Atom.</i>

52:06.581 --> 52:08.333
<i>But the problem is Bora.</i>

52:09.000 --> 52:13.630
<i>Bora will end the earth soon.
Even Atom can't stop him.</i>

52:19.636 --> 52:20.887
We've landed.

52:21.721 --> 52:23.014
Open the hatch.

52:23.640 --> 52:25.016
Here, Professor Ochanomizu.

52:25.100 --> 52:27.477
<i>The air outside is filled with hatred!</i>

52:28.645 --> 52:31.439
<i>Abullah's hatred ate away
all the other emotions</i>

52:31.523 --> 52:33.567
<i>until nothing else was left.</i>

52:34.943 --> 52:37.112
<i>Bora is that hatred itself.</i>

52:37.988 --> 52:40.699
<i>The earth is doomed,
no matter what anyone may try.</i>

52:42.033 --> 52:43.618
That's only in theory.

52:45.704 --> 52:49.166
You've spent too much time in your lab.

52:50.125 --> 52:52.335
You should breathe fresh air
once in a while.

52:53.628 --> 52:56.548
In theory, the earth is doomed.

52:57.215 --> 53:00.302
No matter where we hide,
we're all going to die.

53:02.846 --> 53:07.726
But even in the face of death,
even though we're fully aware of our fate,

53:08.351 --> 53:11.188
we humans never give up hope
until the very end.

53:15.233 --> 53:16.526
<i>Just like Atom.</i>

53:18.236 --> 53:21.698
You are a brilliant scientist, Dr. Tenma.

53:22.949 --> 53:27.787
You created Goji,
but you also created Atom.

53:41.885 --> 53:43.178
What in the--

53:45.138 --> 53:46.181
No one's here?

53:49.684 --> 53:52.062
No response from Orchid City!

53:52.145 --> 53:54.231
Another huge earthquake in Capital Town!

53:54.731 --> 53:59.569
Is this all caused by the crustal movement
in Eden National Park?

53:59.653 --> 54:03.156
Yes, and if an additional
large-scale shock is introduced...

54:03.240 --> 54:04.574
A large-scale shock?

54:04.658 --> 54:08.078
For example,
if an Antiproton Bomb explodes,

54:08.578 --> 54:09.537
then the earth will...

54:11.414 --> 54:13.750
Mr. President, we must declare
a state of emergency!

54:15.126 --> 54:17.045
Mr. President?

54:25.011 --> 54:27.138
We're safe in here, right?

54:28.181 --> 54:30.642
I'm protected here, aren't I?

54:30.725 --> 54:32.894
Yes, I will protect you.

54:36.273 --> 54:37.607
In exchange,

54:38.942 --> 54:41.820
you will be my slave
for the rest of your life.

54:54.207 --> 54:55.208
Atom.

54:55.792 --> 54:57.460
Atom is down there?

54:57.544 --> 55:01.673
He is trying to disable Bora
and the Antiproton Bomb.

55:01.756 --> 55:04.467
Atom can do it, right?

55:04.551 --> 55:05.885
Yes. However,

55:07.304 --> 55:10.056
before he can, his body will melt!

55:25.322 --> 55:26.281
Bora.

55:29.367 --> 55:30.744
Can you hear me, Bora?

55:31.453 --> 55:35.707
Gesicht taught me
that nothing comes from hatred.

55:36.333 --> 55:37.667
Hatred must end.

55:44.424 --> 55:47.344
I tried, but you leave me no choice.
I'll begin.

55:48.011 --> 55:50.305
It'll take five minutes
to disable the bomb.

55:51.181 --> 55:53.600
<i>I have five minutes
until my body starts melting.</i>

55:54.934 --> 55:56.519
In theory, it's impossible.

55:57.729 --> 55:59.731
But I have to give it a try!

56:06.196 --> 56:09.532
I will protect your body.

56:10.575 --> 56:11.493
Sahad.

56:12.077 --> 56:13.495
Let's charge right in.

56:14.371 --> 56:15.205
Okay.

56:25.548 --> 56:28.009
You are mistaken!

56:28.093 --> 56:30.929
Nothing comes from hatred!

56:35.600 --> 56:40.313
Atom, send me the blueprint
of the Antiproton Bomb.

56:40.397 --> 56:41.564
- What?
- Hurry!

57:27.735 --> 57:30.071
Creating fields of flowers,

57:30.613 --> 57:33.074
that was my calling.

57:34.159 --> 57:37.203
I can never be Sahad again.

57:37.912 --> 57:41.207
Atom, please tell Uran for me.

57:41.291 --> 57:42.208
What?

57:43.793 --> 57:47.297
I was glad
we could paint pictures together.

57:47.380 --> 57:49.299
I am grateful!

57:49.382 --> 57:50.508
Sahad!

57:54.512 --> 57:57.307
Sahad!

58:02.687 --> 58:05.607
We must evacuate now!
It could explode at any moment.

58:06.107 --> 58:09.569
Evacuation is pointless.
If it explodes, then the earth will end.

58:14.199 --> 58:15.033
Atom?

58:18.536 --> 58:19.412
Atom!

58:24.876 --> 58:28.379
Atom, take care of the earth for me.

58:34.928 --> 58:36.054
Sahad!

59:37.115 --> 59:38.199
What in the world?

59:39.576 --> 59:41.369
It's the Peltier effect.

59:42.287 --> 59:44.998
When metals
of different properties are joined,

59:45.498 --> 59:47.500
and a high voltage is applied,

59:47.584 --> 59:50.461
sudden heat absorption is induced,

59:50.545 --> 59:53.548
resulting in
an extremely low-temperature state.

59:56.718 --> 59:57.677
Look at the sky!

01:00:08.521 --> 01:00:13.151
How brilliant!
It looks like a field of flowers!

01:00:26.039 --> 01:00:27.123
Pluto.

01:00:27.874 --> 01:00:30.960
No, Sahad saved the earth.

01:00:39.302 --> 01:00:40.178
Atom.

01:00:51.022 --> 01:00:54.150
I only wanted to protect our citizens.

01:00:54.817 --> 01:00:56.986
To protect their future.

01:00:57.987 --> 01:00:59.280
That's all I wanted.

01:01:00.156 --> 01:01:01.199
Oh?

01:01:01.282 --> 01:01:02.450
Something's not right.

01:01:03.910 --> 01:01:05.828
The magma is beginning to subside.

01:01:06.496 --> 01:01:08.081
The explosion has halted.

01:01:09.374 --> 01:01:12.543
Was it Atom? How boring...

01:01:22.762 --> 01:01:23.805
Thank God.

01:01:24.514 --> 01:01:26.057
I'm so glad.

01:01:26.140 --> 01:01:29.352
Well, I can come up with another plan.

01:01:29.435 --> 01:01:31.521
My options are endless.

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:33.773
Please!

01:01:34.273 --> 01:01:38.236
Let us find a way to prosper together
without destroying the human race!

01:01:40.780 --> 01:01:41.864
Who's there?

01:01:53.292 --> 01:01:56.921
Welcome, Brau1589.

01:01:57.004 --> 01:02:01.884
Now, let us begin together.
The creation of our new world.

01:02:02.635 --> 01:02:05.847
So warm. And so weak.

01:02:07.598 --> 01:02:10.810
I see now, Atom.

01:02:15.606 --> 01:02:18.025
Oh dear. What a disappointment.

01:02:18.109 --> 01:02:21.904
I thought you had ascended
to the realm of gods like me.

01:02:46.053 --> 01:02:47.388
This is not the end.

01:02:48.055 --> 01:02:50.892
Unless hatred disappears from the world,

01:02:51.642 --> 01:02:52.769
there will be another...

01:02:54.520 --> 01:02:58.191
Professor, will we ever see a day
when there is no hatred?

01:02:58.941 --> 01:03:00.067
I don't know.

01:03:00.777 --> 01:03:02.904
We can only hope that day will come.

01:03:05.907 --> 01:03:06.783
Mont Blanc,

01:03:07.408 --> 01:03:08.326
North No.2,

01:03:09.202 --> 01:03:10.077
Brando,

01:03:10.703 --> 01:03:11.537
Hercules,

01:03:12.371 --> 01:03:13.247
Epsilon,

01:03:13.956 --> 01:03:14.832
Gesicht,

01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.585
and Sahad...

01:03:19.045 --> 01:03:20.922
I'm sure they're praying

01:03:21.964 --> 01:03:23.549
for that day to come.

01:03:26.803 --> 01:03:27.720
All of them.

01:06:00.289 --> 01:06:03.960
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
